## Reclassification on a higher-ranking event

When another documented maturity event occurs on a loan whose Maturity and Due-and-Payable Cases case is open, and the new event ranks higher in supersede priority than the case's current event type:

- the case is reclassified to the new event type and event date while keeping its status and deadlines;
- from then on the new type's settings govern;
- a death or sale removes any cure option.

## Death on a Summit loan's open case

Where the death of the last surviving borrower supersedes another maturity event on a Cedarline Summit loan's open case, and only for such a case, the case:

- is reclassified to the Death of Last Surviving Borrower plan, with the date of death as its event date;
- keeps its status and its response deadline;
- has its resolution deadline carried forward by the successor runway days;
- from then on is governed by the death plan's settings, with no cure option.

| Case situation | Event type after reclassification | Event date | Status and response deadline | Resolution deadline |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Summit loan, open case, last surviving borrower dies | Death of Last Surviving Borrower | date of death | kept | carried forward by the successor runway days |
| any loan, open case, higher-ranking event other than that one | the new event type | the new event date | kept | kept |

## Booking the reclassification: `reclassify_case_to_death_eeacbce3`

**Capability.** One call does three things:

- changes the case's maturity event type to Death of Last Surviving Borrower;
- replaces the case's event date with the date of death supplied;
- moves the case's resolution deadline later by the runway days supplied. A value of 0 leaves the deadline where it is.

The case keeps its status, its due-and-payable date and its response deadline. Afterwards the case lookup shows the new event type, event date and resolution deadline.

**Invocation.** This is an agent-side tool. The agent unlocks `reclassify_case_to_death_eeacbce3` and then calls it.

**Parameters.**

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `maturity_case_id` | reference number of the open maturity case being reclassified, as returned by the maturity case lookup for the deceased borrower | identifier |
| `event_date` | the borrower's date of death, which becomes the case's event date | calendar date YYYY-MM-DD, no time or time zone; may not be empty |
| `runway_days_added` | whole number of calendar days by which the case's current resolution deadline is moved later | integer of 0 or more, no unit text, no decimals |

**Return.** A text rendering of a record with these fields:

- `maturity_case_id`;
- `variant_name`, the case's resulting event type;
- `event_date`;
- `previous_resolution_deadline`, the deadline the case carried when the call was made;
- `resolution_deadline`, the case's resulting deadline;
- `runway_days_added`, the days applied.

A receipt carrying the case reference number and the event type Death of Last Surviving Borrower means the reclassification is recorded. If no case has the reference given, the call returns an error naming that reference.
